    {
      "dom_id": "question-183569",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "There is a real number such that, added to any natural number, gives a positive number.\n\nExpress the above in formal language.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that our sentence can be re-phrased as \n\nThere exists a real number $x$ such that, added to any natural number, gives a positive number.\n\nNow, \"$x$ added to any natural number gives a positive number\" means that\n\nFor any natural number $n,$ we have that $x+n>0.$\n\nTherefore, we get the following statement:\n\nThere exists a real number $x$ such that for any natural number $n$ we have that $x+n>0.$\n\nMore formally, this reads as\n\n$∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,x+n>0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
